From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PanfrostMesa26 <mesa26@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 10:30:00
Subject: [PATCH 0138] gpu31-panfrost: DRM 1.1 + Mesa 26 GET_PARAM/flags uapi

Mesa 26's panfrost/kmod backend (same code as the local 27.0-devel tree)
refuses this driver before any ioctl: panfrost_kmod_dev_create() requires
drmGetVersion() >= 1.1.  It then queries a feature set through GET_PARAM
(required=true: a failed query is an assert in debug builds and zeros in
release builds, which breaks the compiler) and passes modern CREATE_BO flags.

- drm_driver major/minor 1.0 -> 1.1.  Deliberately 1.1 and not higher: 1.3
  adds SYSTEM_TIMESTAMP, 1.4 SET_LABEL_BO and 1.6 QUERY_BO_INFO (Mesa would
  switch the import path to an ioctl this table does not implement).  1.1
  gives BO_HEAP/NOEXEC flags + GET_BO_OFFSET imports, which this driver has.
- Feature snapshot at probe (block is powered there), read with the mainline
  panfrost_gpu_init_features() offsets: GPU_ID, L2/CORE/TILER/MEM/MMU
  features, AS/JS present, THREAD_FEATURES, MAX_THREADS, max workgroup /
  barrier, COHERENCY, AFBC (0x4C), 4 texture features, JS features per
  present slot, shader/tiler/l2/stack present (LO|HI<<32), TLS alloc,
  nr_core_groups = hweight64(l2_present).  GET_PARAM answers all of them
  from this snapshot; the 1.3/1.5/1.6-only ids stay -EINVAL (Mesa tolerates
  because it gates them on the version).  Every query is logged with id,
  value and rc, so the device run shows exactly which ids Mesa 26 asks for.
- CREATE_BO: keep size==0 (and now pad!=0) rejected; accept
  PANFROST_BO_NOEXEC (1) and PANFROST_BO_HEAP (2), accept PANFROST_BO_WB_MMAP
  (4) as a no-op (backing is pre-faulted SHMEM either way), and warn-ignore
  any unknown bit instead of -EINVAL.  One enter log with args->flags plus
  sizeof/flags/pad/offset offsets proves the uapi layout on the device.
  MMAP_BO flags are warn-ignored too (currently no meaning).
- uapi: enum drm_panfrost_param gains the modern ids in upstream order
  (through SELECTED_COHERENCY; GPU_PROD_ID stays 0) and the PANFROST_BO_*
  defines; struct layouts are unchanged (verified by the enter log).

Diagnostic prints are one line per ioctl/probe and can be dropped later.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drm.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drm.h
